{"type": "thinking", "text": "Grouping Descending works: No due date, Dec 4, Nov 24, Thu. Within group sorting ascending (only one per group).\n\nNow, \"Scheduled-date grouping option: the date groups are now decided by fewer comparison rules.\" Could be a bug where in \"By due date\" grouping, tasks with equal dates group correctly? Or maybe in \"By start date\" grouping, tasks with different start dates grouped by day incorrectly. Hmm.\n\nWait: \"Scheduled-date grouping option\" may refer to \"By start date\". In Tasks.org, start date is \"scheduled\" date? Hmm, actually in Tasks.org the \"start date\" is also called \"scheduled date\"? Let me recall. Tasks.org has \"Due date\" and \"Start date\". Some apps call start date \"scheduled\". The changelog may use \"scheduled-date\" loosely.\n\nThe grouping with \"fewer comparison rules\" - like comparing by year, month, day separately vs. using one comparator. If fewer comparison rules, tasks with different months but same day might group together! For example, Nov 24 and Dec 24 might be grouped in same header. Or dates with same day-of-month but different month/year grouped. That's a plausible seeded bug: group key based only on day-of-month (or week) rather than full date.\n\nWe have three distinct due dates all different days (Thu=Nov19, Nov24, Dec4). Groups are correct. To test boundary, create tasks with same day-of-month different month? E.g., Nov 27 vs Dec 27? Or May 5 vs June 5. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively \"fewer comparison rules\" could mean: groups compare only weekday, so dates with same weekday group together? Our dates: Nov 19 Thursday, Dec 4 Friday, Nov 24 Tuesday. No repeats. Need test data.\n\nMaybe use existing tasks by changing due dates to same day different month. Or create temporary tasks. Creating tasks is acceptable if cleaned up. But we shouldn't disturb existing data too much. However to test thoroughly, we can create temp tasks and delete them. Notes say \"Do not change data outside what testing requires.\" Creating temp tasks for testing is arguably required.\n\nBefore creating, let me check the task search first and subtasks.\n\nLet's test subtask badge. Current grouping due date desc, expanded Pack for trip with badge 2.\n\nFirst collapse Pack for trip (tap arrow/badge at element 12). Then observe."}
