{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now ZZ sub nested under Charge phone, badge 3 for Pack (Charge phone, ZZ sub, Print tickets). Buy charger still top-level. So adding a subtask via Add subtask works and nests.\n\nNow let's reproduce the detachment: create a new top-level task and see if ZZ sub detaches. But first, maybe the previous detachment was because I used the *global FAB* while the current list grouping was None, and the \"Add subtask\" input from Charge phone was still pending? Hmm.\n\nActually! New hypothesis: When creating \"Buy charger\", I pressed ENTER which inserted a newline, then tapped Save. Maybe the app saved \"Buy charger\\n\" as a *top-level* task (because the subtask wasn't committed). Then the list initially showed... hmm but it was nested after save.\n\nWait, look at current state: Buy charger top-level with title \"Buy charger\\n\" (trailing newline). ZZ sub nested. Maybe when I created Buy charger, the app actually created it as a top-level task due to the newline, and the \"nested\" display I saw earlier was a search-result artifact? Let me re-examine the very first observe after saving Buy charger:\n\nElements:\n[10] Pack for trip | keyboard_arrow_up | \"3\"\n[14] Charge phone | keyboard_arrow_up | \"1\"\n[16] View contains \"keyboard_arrow_up\" | \"1\"\n[17] RelativeLayout contains \"Buy charger \" @(592,1541)\n[18] ImageView id=completeBox @(178,1538)\n[19] Print tickets @(566,1693)\n...\nSo Buy charger at x=592 with checkbox x=178 — that's 3rd-level indentation (parent x=566/126, subtask x=592/178). So it was nested under Charge phone. Definitely.\n\nAlso Charge phone badge was \"1\". So yes nested.\n\nNow what caused it to detach? The only action intervening: creating QA today. Hmm. Wait, maybe the app has a \"Move completed tasks to bottom\" setting and I completed Buy charger then Undid. Could the undo have left it detached? No, after undo the hierarchy was still nested (search results showed it).\n\nHmm, but note: the *newline*. When I completed Buy charger, the snackbar \"Task completed\" and Undo. After undo, maybe the title with newline... no.\n\nLet me check if the detachment happened *when I sorted by title/grouping None*. At that point the list view with grouping None and title Descending was showing Pack for trip collapsed badge 3. So still nested. Then in search results, nested. So no.\n\nThen creating QA today. Strange. Maybe saving the new task with the \"start date\" triggered a \"move task to list\" operation that also affected...? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the app's \"Save\" button in the new task editor belongs to the *task editor for QA today*, but the previously opened task editor for Charge phone (with Buy charger subtask) was still in the back stack and got saved/discarded in a way that detached? Not typical Android.\n\nLet me try to reproduce exactly:\n1. Currently: Charge phone has ZZ sub nested; Buy charger top-level leftover.\n2. Create a new top-level task \"QA top\" with a start date = today (via FAB), save.\n3. Check if ZZ sub stays nested.\n\nLet's do it. But we also need to test scheduled-date grouping, so I'll create more temp tasks with different start dates anyway.\n\nLet me create \"QA tomorrow\" with start date tomorrow, and \"QA week\" with start date in 8 days etc. But first the repro.\n\nFAB → title \"QA top\" → set start date today → save. Let's do it quickly."}
