{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now interesting: After saving \"QA top\", the list shows:\n[2] ZZ sub TOP-LEVEL (x=540, checkbox x=73)\n[4] Read docs\n[6] QA top\n[8] QA today\n[10] Pay rent\n[13] Pack for trip badge 2 (collapsed)\n[21] Buy milk\n[24] Buy charger\n\nSo ZZ sub got detached from Charge phone! Reproduced! The pattern: creating and saving a new task detaches the most recently added subtask (ZZ sub) and promotes it to top-level. Also Pack badge went from 3 to 2 (Charge phone, Print tickets only). Charge phone's subtask ZZ sub is now top-level.\n\nWait, also sorting is by title Descending with grouping None. Order: ZZ sub (Z), Read docs (R), QA top, QA today, Pay rent, Pack for trip, Buy milk, Buy charger. Yes alphabetical descending. So ZZ sub is top-level now.\n\nHmm, so is this a real bug? It seems like saving a new task causes the last-added subtask to detach. That's bizarre. Could it instead be that the app considers the new task as \"sibling\" of the subtask due to a bug in the \"add subtask\" flow? Wait — maybe ZZ sub was never actually a subtask; maybe when I pressed Save on Charge phone, it saved but the subtask input remained in \"draft\" and got committed later on the next save? Hmm, but after saving Charge phone with ZZ sub, the list showed ZZ sub nested under Charge phone. So it was nested.\n\nThen saving QA top detached it. Could this be caused by the fact that the previous save (Charge phone) left an active draft subtask item in a global state, and the next \"Save\" commits it as top-level? Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the app's task editor has a \"Save\" that saves all tasks; the subtask draft \"ZZ sub\" was saved nested. When opening a new task editor and saving, maybe it also re-saves the previous parent without the subtask (detaching it). That sounds like a bug in the app's data layer/editor.\n\nBut wait, in the first occurrence, Buy charger was detached by saving QA today (which had a start date). Now ZZ sub detached by saving QA top (also with start date). Coincidence? Both new tasks had start dates. Maybe the start date setting is relevant: the app may treat the new task's start date and reorder... no.\n\nLet me test once more with a new task WITHOUT setting a start date to isolate. Create \"QA plain\" and save; see if anything detaches. Currently Charge phone has no subtasks (ZZ sub detached). If I add a subtask ZY then save; then create plain task without start date and see. But maybe simpler: create \"QA plain\" and save; check if \"Buy charger\" or anything changes. Hmm, currently Charge phone no subtasks, so nothing to detach except... the top-level tasks.\n\nActually, the detachment might be a bug caused by sorting/grouping \"None\" + some \"My order\" thing. Wait, when I saved QA top, the list re-sorted alphabetically (title descending). The subtask ZZ sub moved and became top-level. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the \"detachment\" is not data corruption but a *display* issue: With grouping None + sorting, subtasks are displayed as top-level rows (flat), and parent's badge shows only direct non-detached? Let's check: Charge phone row after saving QA top shows no badge (meaning no subtasks). Before saving, Charge phone had badge 1. So data changed.\n\nBut maybe the badge is not shown because the list is flat and shows \"ZZ sub\" as a row? Hmm, the parent Charge phone no longer shows badge. And Pack badge 2 (Charge phone, Print tickets). Earlier Pack badge 3 (Charge phone, ZZ sub, Print tickets). So yes data change.\n\nThis looks like a real bug: saving a new task causes a subtask to be reparented to top level. But is it within \"subtasks\" area? Yes! \"Subtask badges\" specifically. Hmm, but the bug is about subtask hierarchy.\n\nHowever, I'm not sure the cause is \"saving a new task\". Let me test a cleaner reproduction that doesn't rely on weird state.\n\nNew controlled test:\n1. Add subtask \"QQ child\" under Charge phone and save. Verify nested (Charge badge 1, Pack badge 3).\n2. Create a brand-new task \"QQ plain\" (no start date), save. Verify whether QQ child stays nested.\n\nLet's do it.\n\nFirst, expand Pack for trip (currently collapsed). Tap badge 15."}
