{"type": "thinking", "text": "QA month (Dec 14) got its own group \"Start Monday, December 14\", separate from \"Start today\" (Nov 14). So the date grouping by start date is correct for same day-of-month different month. No bug there.\n\nBut wait: the change says \"date groups are now decided by fewer comparison rules.\" Maybe the bug only concerns the \"By start date\" grouping when start dates are in the same week but different days? We have today/tomorrow/Nov 24/Dec 14 all separate. Groups correct.\n\nHmm. Maybe the scheduled-date grouping refers to *due date* grouping? The term \"scheduled-date\" might map to due date? But \"By due date\" grouping already tested: groups Thu, Nov 24, Dec 4, No due date, separate. Are there any anomalies? \"Due Thursday\" vs \"Due Tuesday, November 24\": the first group header omits month/day and just \"Due Thursday\". Could that be the \"fewer comparison rules\" bug? Hmm no.\n\nWait, maybe \"Scheduled-date grouping option\" is a new option that groups due dates into ranges like \"Overdue\", \"Today\", \"Tomorrow\", \"This week\", \"Next week\", \"Later\". But the grouping options we saw: None, By due date, By start date, By priority, By last modified, Created, List. Hmm.\n\nActually, Tasks.org recently added \"Group by date\" option? There's \"Grouping: By due date\" and \"By start date\". The changed \"Scheduled-date grouping option\" likely refers to \"By start date\" (scheduled). Our test shows correct groups.\n\nBut the hint says \"date groups are now decided by fewer comparison rules\" — maybe the bug is that groups are decided by only the day-of-week, causing Dec 14 (Monday) and Dec 21 (Monday) to merge? We tested Dec 14 vs Nov 14 (same day-of-month) — didn't merge. Let's test same weekday? \"fewer comparison rules\" could mean comparing only the calendar date's *day* (e.g., `getDayOfMonth`), which we disproved. Or comparing only the week-of-year? Hmm.\n\nMaybe it compares only the year and day-of-year? Unlikely.\n\nLet's look at the group headers: \"Start today\", \"Start tomorrow\", \"Start Tuesday, November 24\", \"Start Monday, December 14\", \"No start date\". The date format changes: within 1 day relative, \"today/tomorrow\"; else weekday + month day. It's based on `formatDate`. \"fewer comparison rules\" might mean the function that decides whether to show \"Today\"/\"Tomorrow\" vs full date now only checks a subset of fields, causing dates like Dec 14 to be labeled \"Start today\" (if only comparing day-of-month 14!). But Dec 14 got \"Start Monday, December 14\" — correct, so not that.\n\nHmm, wait: what about a date exactly one year away (Nov 14, 2027)? If comparison only checks month/day (fewer rules), it might label it \"Start today\"! That's plausible: date formatting for \"Today\" might compare only month and day (not year). But that's not grouping, that's label. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, the group *keys* may be the formatted date string, and two dates with the same formatted string merge; with fewer comparison rules, the format might omit the year, so Nov 14 2026 and Nov 14 2027 would have the same group key \"Start today\"/\"Start Saturday, November 14\" without year. Let's test with a start date one year ahead (Nov 14, 2027). That's a plausible boundary test. But creating such a task requires switching the year in the date picker (tap \"November 2026\" → year selection). Doable but long.\n\nMaybe there's a more likely seeded bug: grouping start dates by only month+day would merge Nov 14 2026 and Nov 14 2027, yes. Let's test that. If merged, it's the \"fewer comparison rules\" bug. But would users hit it? It's an edge case. QA sweep expects boundary tests, so yes.\n\nAlternatively, compare only \"day of month\" would merge Nov 14 with Dec 14—we disproved. Comparing month+day would merge across years. Let's test.\n\nActually, the changelog phrase \"date groups are now decided by fewer comparison rules\" suggests the comparison function used to compare more fields (year, month, day) and now compares fewer. If it used to compare year+month+day+time, and now compares only month+day (or just day), then dates in different years/months could merge. Our test with same day different month shows it compares month too. So the remaining possibility is year omitted. That's a classic bug: formatting the group header without year (or comparing formatted date without year) causes dates a year apart to merge. Let's test by creating \"QA year\" with start date Nov 14, 2027.\n\nSetting year 2027 in the picker: tap \"November 2026\" (or with switch year), then choose year. Let's attempt. Create task FAB → title \"QA year\" → start date → tap \"November 2026\" title → year selector. Let's see.\n\nActually, maybe I can avoid creating a new task by editing an existing temp task \"QA plain\" to have start date Nov 14, 2027. Either way similar steps.\n\nLet's create \"QA year\". FAB element 29."}
