(Low). That's inconsistent. Could be a bug in the task editor: default priority for new tasks is Low instead of None. But is that one of the changed areas? Not mentioned. But it might explain the grouping: all our temp tasks (created via FAB) have Low priority, while original tasks (Buy milk, Pack, etc.) have None. But the group header shows \"Low priority\" and the list under it includes original tasks? Let's check: The visible list under \"Low priority\" includes Buy charger (temp), QA month (temp), QA next (temp), QA plain.. (temp), QA today (temp), QA tomorrow (temp), QA top (temp), QA year (temp). It may also include original tasks further down. If original tasks have None priority, they should be in a different group. But we only see one header \"Low priority\" — maybe the next group is below (scroll). Let's scroll down to see if there's another header (e.g., \"No priority\"). The visible list has no header after \"Low priority\" at top. Scroll down."}
