{"type": "thinking", "text": "Search special chars works.\n\nNow maybe test search query with leading/trailing space \"milk \" — should still match. Not necessary.\n\nLet's test the subtask badge behavior with \"Show completed subtasks\" off and a completed subtask, to see if badge count matches \"full list\". Actually, let's think of what the badge bug might be besides detach. The changelog says badge computed from full list of nested tasks. We verified 4 for two-level nesting. So the feature works. The detach bug is separate but affects it.\n\nMaybe there is another seeded bug in the badge: when a task has a *completed* nested subtask and \"Show completed subtasks\" is off, badge should not count it? Hmm. Let's test quickly to see if any inconsistency: complete BB grandchild and hide completed subtasks. Pack badge = ? If it still shows 4, and hidden completed grandchild, maybe should show 3. But ambiguous.\n\nWe already have one confirmed bug, and likely the seeded bugs for other areas either don't exist or are subtle. Let's consider the \"Sort sheet: direction preference now loaded with a new fallback value\" bug once more. Could there be a UI mismatch when the sort sheet is opened *after rotating to landscape*? In landscape, the sheet only showed 13 elements, missing \"Move completed tasks to bottom\" and \"Completed\" rows. Maybe due to scroll, not bug.\n\nMaybe the direction fallback bug: \"Sort sheet: the direction preference is now loaded with a new fallback value.\" If the fallback is, say, `ASC` for all modes, then for \"By priority\" etc. we'd see Ascending. But we saw By priority Descending, Created Descending, last modified Descending. So per-mode defaults. Looks fine.\n\nWhat about `Grouping` direction fallback? For grouping By priority, direction Descending (we saw). For By due date, Ascending. For By start date, Ascending. Fine.\n\nMaybe the fallback value is the *wrong type* causing the direction to be \"Descending\" for grouping By title? There's no grouping by title. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the bug manifests only for the \"Sorting\" row when the sort mode is \"My order\" (disabled) or \"Smart sort\". We saw Smart sort Descending. Fine.\n\nLet's test toggling direction then switching mode and back for Sorting to see if preference is remembered per mode (maybe expected). If it is not remembered, maybe that's the bug. But as discussed, not clearly a bug.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the direction preference is global, and the bug is that switching sort mode keeps the previous direction (shouldn't). We observed switching from By due date Descending to By title showed Ascending (default reset), so not keeping.\n\nI think the direction area is clean.\n\nNow let's test grouping \"By last modified\" and \"List\" quickly for major breakage. Since all tasks are in Default list, \"List\" grouping should show \"Default list\" header (or \"None\"?). Let's test \"List\". Open sort, grouping List. But this may not be necessary. Still, \"sorting and grouping options\" is a listed area; we should exercise all grouping options at least once. We tested None, By due date, By start date, By priority. Not yet By last modified, Created, List. Let's do them quickly.\n\nCurrently search active. Exit search (tap Collapse 37) then sort."}
