{"type": "thinking", "text": "The 9 selected were deleted. Remaining temp tasks: QQ child, RR child, SS child, TT child, ZZ sub (top-level, in \"Modified today\" group), and AA child, BB grandchild nested under Charge phone. Also Buy charger, QA tasks deleted.\n\nBut wait! The \"Modified today\" group now shows QQ child, RR child, SS child, TT child, ZZ sub, then \"No date\" header with Buy milk, Pack for trip...\n\nHmm, \"No date\" header?! That's odd: grouping By last modified Descending, the groups should be \"Modified today\", \"Modified ...\" not \"No date\". Wait, the header at element 13 says \"No date\" — that's weird. Actually, maybe the grouping is now By due date? We had set grouping By last modified, but after deleting tasks maybe... Hmm, \"No date\" is not a last-modified group label. Did our action mode delete somehow change grouping? Let's check: Earlier we set grouping By last modified Descending; list showed \"Modified today\". After deleting, the list shows \"Modified today\" group then \"No date\" header. Could \"No date\" be a last-modified group? No. Wait, maybe the sorting/grouping changed due to something else. Let's not worry; we'll reset at the end.\n\nActually, \"No date\" might be the header for tasks with no *due date* if grouping is By due date. But we set By last modified. Hmm. Maybe the deletion of tasks triggered a settings change? Unlikely. Let's verify the sort sheet later.\n\nNow, the snackbar says \"0 deleted\" even though 9 selected tasks were deleted. This confirms the wrong count bug even more strongly! The developer couldn't reproduce, but here 9 tasks were deleted and it says 0 deleted. Wait — maybe \"0 deleted\" is counting *completed* tasks? No. It's clearly the deletion feedback and it's wrong. Maybe the count is the number of tasks the app *failed* to delete? It says 0 deleted, and indeed some selected tasks may not have been deleted (QQ child, RR child, etc. weren't selected). But the 9 selected were deleted. Hmm.\n\nActually, wait: The snackbar \"0 deleted\" might be a *persistent* snackbar from the previous deletion that didn't disappear because the app doesn't dismiss it? The snackbar at the bottom might be from the previous operation (deleting QA plain2). But we just performed a new delete; the snackbar should update. It could be a stale snackbar that wasn't replaced? Hmm. After the first delete, snackbar \"0 deleted\" appeared. Then we did long-press and selection (snackbar may have timed out in ~4 seconds). During selection, the snackbar wasn't visible in the observe. After the second delete, \"0 deleted\" appeared again. So it's the new snackbar. Still wrong.\n\nGiven the developer couldn't reproduce, maybe the count semantics are different: maybe \"0 deleted\" is the number of *tasks deleted from other lists*? Or maybe the app shows \"0 deleted\" because deletion is actually done via a \"trash\" and the count is something else. Regardless, it's misleading. But since it's out of scope and rejected, we can drop it.\n\nNote: We still have temp tasks QQ child, RR child, SS child, TT child, ZZ sub, AA child, BB grandchild. Let's delete them too. These are top-level except AA and BB. We can select the top-level ones now: QQ child, RR child, SS child, TT child, ZZ sub (5 tasks) in the \"Modified today\" group. Then AA child & BB grandchild (nested under Charge phone) — select those separately.\n\nLet's long-press QQ child (3) and tap RR child (5), SS child (7), TT child (9), ZZ sub (11). Note the list may scroll? It's static. Let's do long-press then taps in one block."}
